---
import Navigation from '../layouts/Navigation.astro';
---
<html lang="en"><head><meta charset="utf-8"/><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width"/><title>Ferris | Evidence</title></head>
<body><Navigation/><nav><b>ferris</b><span>Earth investigations</span></nav><main><header><small>THE EARTH DATA DETECTIVE</small><h1>Follow the change.<br/>Question the evidence.</h1><p>Explore a vegetation signal, examine its uncertainty, and investigate what comes next.</p></header><div class="layout"><article><small class="notice">ILLUSTRATIVE EXAMPLE · SYNTHETIC VALUES</small><h2>Vegetation greenness</h2><p>2017–2025 · Annual NDVI · Illustrative region</p><div id="chart" role="img" aria-label="Synthetic NDVI observations and fitted trend"></div><div class="metrics"><div>Slope per year<strong id="slope"></strong></div><div>OLS p-value<strong id="p"></strong></div><div>95% slope interval<strong id="ci"></strong></div></div><h3>What does this mean?</h3><p id="meaning"></p><button id="why">Why this result? ↗</button> <button id="export">Download evidence</button><details><summary>Observations and method</summary><p>Ordinary least squares with Student t inference. Annual synthetic values. No seasonal adjustment applied.</p><table><thead><tr><th>Year</th><th>NDVI</th></tr></thead><tbody id="rows"></tbody></table></details></article><aside><h2>Investigate the evidence</h2><div class="tabs"><button data-panel="stats">Statistics</button><button data-panel="satellite">Satellite</button><button data-panel="next">Next step</button></div><section id="stats"><small>STATISTICAL EXPLANATION</small><h3>How strong is the signal?</h3><p id="explain"></p><h4>Assumptions and quality</h4><p>Independent errors, constant variance and approximately normal residuals. Nine annual observations provide limited diagnostic power.</p><p id="quality"></p><p>NDVI describes vegetation greenness. Its increase alone cannot establish an increase in forest cover. Rainfall, crop cycles and land management are possible explanations.</p></section><section id="satellite" hidden><small>SATELLITE EVIDENCE</small><h3>Inspect the landscape</h3><p>This synthetic mission has no associated satellite scenes. A real investigation needs georeferenced imagery from comparable seasons.</p><ol><li>Retrieve HLS red and near-infrared reflectance.</li><li>Mask clouds and shadows.</li><li>Align scenes and compute NDVI differences.</li><li>Record scene IDs and valid coverage.</li></ol><a href="https://hls.gsfc.nasa.gov/data-access-and-tools/">Explore NASA HLS data ↗</a></section><section id="next" hidden><small>FOLLOW-UP INVESTIGATION</small><h3>Did rainfall change too?</h3><p>Compare rainfall and vegetation over shared dates and the same region. Examine seasonal cycles and plausible response lags.</p><p>This rule-based suggestion is a hypothesis to test. A rainfall relationship has not been measured for this fixture.</p><a href="https://gpm.nasa.gov/data/imerg">Explore NASA IMERG ↗</a></section></aside></div><footer>Ferris · Evidence before interpretation</footer></main>
<script>
import * as echarts from 'echarts';
const d=await fetch('/evidence.json').then(r=>r.json());
function put(id:string,text:string){document.getElementById(id)!.textContent=text}
put('slope','+'+d.slope.toFixed(4));put('p',d.p.toPrecision(3));put('ci',d.interval.map((v:number)=>v.toFixed(4)).join(' to '));
put('meaning','In this synthetic series, the fitted NDVI slope is '+d.slope.toFixed(4)+' units per year. It '+(d.p<.05?'meets':'does not meet')+' the 0.05 significance threshold under the stated model assumptions.');
put('explain','The fitted line explains '+(d.r2*100).toFixed(1)+'% of variation. The p-value describes how unusual a slope this extreme would be under a zero-slope model and its assumptions. It does not give the probability that a hypothesis is true.');
put('quality',d.n+' observations; '+d.missing+' missing. NASA quality flags are unavailable for synthetic data.');
document.getElementById('rows')!.innerHTML=d.years.map((y:number,i:number)=>'<tr><td>'+y+'</td><td>'+d.values[i].toFixed(3)+'</td></tr>').join('');
const chart=echarts.init(document.getElementById('chart'));
chart.setOption({animation:false,tooltip:{trigger:'axis'},legend:{bottom:0},grid:{left:45,right:15,top:30,bottom:65},xAxis:{type:'category',data:d.years},yAxis:{name:'NDVI',min:.42,max:.63},series:[{name:'Observed',type:'line',data:d.values,itemStyle:{color:'#25684d'},symbolSize:8},{name:'Fitted',type:'line',data:d.fitted,symbol:'none',lineStyle:{type:'dashed',color:'#b16d37'}},{name:'95% lower mean bound',type:'line',data:d.lower,symbol:'none',lineStyle:{color:'#aabdab',width:1}},{name:'95% upper mean bound',type:'line',data:d.upper,symbol:'none',lineStyle:{color:'#aabdab',width:1}}]});
new ResizeObserver(()=>chart.resize()).observe(document.getElementById('chart')!);
function select(id:string){['stats','satellite','next'].forEach(p=>document.getElementById(p)!.hidden=p!==id);document.querySelectorAll<HTMLButtonElement>('[data-panel]').forEach(b=>b.setAttribute('aria-pressed',String(b.dataset.panel===id)));}
document.querySelectorAll<HTMLButtonElement>('[data-panel]').forEach(b=>b.onclick=()=>select(b.dataset.panel!));select('stats');
document.getElementById('why')!.onclick=()=>{select('stats');document.querySelector<HTMLButtonElement>('[data-panel=stats]')!.focus()};
document.getElementById('export')!.onclick=()=>{const u=URL.createObjectURL(new Blob([JSON.stringify(d,null,2)],{type:'application/json'}));const a=document.createElement('a');a.href=u;a.download='ferris-synthetic-evidence.json';a.click();setTimeout(()=>URL.revokeObjectURL(u),1000)};
</script>
<style is:global>
@import url('https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=DM+Sans:wght@400;500;700&family=Instrument+Serif&display=swap');
*{box-sizing:border-box}body{margin:0;background:#f2f3ed;color:#263d32;font-family:'DM Sans',sans-serif;line-height:1.6}nav{padding:20px 5%;border-bottom:1px solid #d3dbcf;display:flex;justify-content:space-between}nav b{font-size:28px}main{max-width:1400px;margin:auto;padding:45px 5%}header{max-width:730px;margin-bottom:35px}h1{font-family:'Instrument Serif',serif;font-weight:400;font-size:clamp(42px,5vw,70px);line-height:1.05;margin:16px 0}h2{font-size:25px;margin-bottom:0}small{font-size:11px;letter-spacing:1.5px}p{font-size:15px}.notice{color:#8b5b28}.layout{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1.7fr 1fr;gap:24px}article,aside{padding:28px;border-radius:18px;border:1px solid #dbe2d5;background:white}aside{background:#e6eddf}#chart{height:340px;width:100%}.metrics{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr 1.3fr;gap:12px;border-block:1px solid #dbe2d5;padding:20px 0;font-size:11px}strong{display:block;font-size:22px}.metrics>div:last-child strong{font-size:16px}button{cursor:pointer;border:0;border-radius:7px;padding:10px 14px;background:#275e44;color:white;font:inherit;font-size:13px}.tabs{display:flex;gap:5px;flex-wrap:wrap;margin:20px 0}.tabs button{background:transparent;color:#275e44}.tabs button[aria-pressed=true]{background:white}details{margin-top:25px}summary{cursor:pointer}table{width:100%;text-align:left}td,th{padding:5px;border-bottom:1px solid #ddd}a{color:#216248}footer{margin-top:25px;font-size:12px}button:focus-visible{outline:3px solid #bd7637;outline-offset:3px}[hidden]{display:none}@media(max-width:850px){.layout{grid-template-columns:1fr}article,aside{padding:20px}}
</style></body></html>
